{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1487871-quantum-psionic-interactions","id":1487871,"title":"Quantum & Psionic Interactions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-25T05:16:42-07:00","id":1487871,"title":"Quantum & Psionic Interactions.","content":"Are there any guidelines on how these interact? The Aeon book buts everything into PSI/Taint and the Aberrant book turns everything into Quantum powers. What I want to know is how they interact. What happens when you try to use quantum leech on a Psion? Does it just fail? Does it steal Psi? Things like that. It seems like this should be a sidebar somewhere but I can't find anything for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T05:23:03-07:00","id":1487872,"title":"","content":"No rules describing but some general descriptions:<br /> - Quantum can't sense or command Psi.<br /> - Psi can sense, but not command Quantum without QK.<br /> <br /> As I understand you cant drain Psi using Quantum Leech, the same way you can drain Inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:09:45-07:00","id":1487902,"title":"","content":"I think there's something in Aeon about psi powers incurring increased difficulty when used directly against an aberrant, but don't have time to look for a reference as I need to leave for work in five minutes. For a quick house rule, I'd say you should increase the difficulty by the penalty the aberrant takes to social interactions with baseline humans; the higher their Transcendence, the harder it becomes to affect them with psi, and normal humans, who have psi 1, subconsciously pick up on this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:57:33-07:00","id":1487916,"title":"","content":"Transcendence (corruption) make it harder to use powers directly in Novas. That is how I houserule it to make it less impactful in aPsiads in Nova Era game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T17:16:38-07:00","id":1487952,"title":"","content":"The short version is they are vaguely antagonistic, though for MOST Psi enabled beings, this isn't a huge deal... but Psi can sense (but usually somewhat fuzzily) Quantum, but Quantum can neither sense nor affect Psi... though, I would allow a modified form of Quantum Disruption where you disrupt Psi, but in a different fashion, probably raising Difficulty or creating a Complication on an area/person for Psi, rather than targeting a power. But it'd be difficult and be pretty much like tossing a heavy blanket or net over the targets. And you couldn't choose to ignore some if you had Psi using allies and affected a whole area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T18:03:38-07:00","id":1487956,"title":"","content":"It seems kind of strange in that they aren't technically opposites, but more like compliments (and we have QK to prove that). Psiads/Psions can sense quantum as &quot;taint/corruption/static&quot; even though it's supposed to be a fundamental force in the universe. Novas can't sense psi, but it seems like they'd detect the absence of quantum, perhaps they'd look at a psi-user and see a blank space or black hole where quantum signature should be?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}